    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2037247082684088592",
      "url": "https://x.com/donaldgorbachev/status/2037247082684088592",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/donaldgorbachev/status/2037247082684088592",
      "text": "The five-second epistemology of the nerds discovering the bullwhip.\nCascading multiplicative effects from the physical scarcity of oil in global markets. Look at all the big words. Cascading. Multiplicative. Physical scarcity. The nerds found a thesaurus. It’s called a bullwhip. One word. The kitchen said it on Day 3. The purchasing manager cancels the safety stock because the jawboning said productive conversations. The jawboning expires. The purchasing manager re-orders into a market that moved against him. The re-order is larger because the fear is larger. The amplification amplifies. The cascade cascades. The multiplicative multiplies. One word. Bullwhip. The nerds writing a dissertation on the thing the kitchen named in one word.\n\nThere will be pain. There is pain. Slovenia is rationing. The Philippines declared a national energy emergency. Shell said Europe faces shortages next month. Hapag-Lloyd can’t rescue its own team. Turkey just dumped $8 billion in gold. The DFL at an all-time high in twenty-six years of data. 24 million barrels per day net deficit bigger than COVID. The pain isn’t coming. The pain moved in. The pain redecorated. The pain changed the locks. The nerds saying there will be pain the way The Economist says could weaken for years. Arriving at the present tense using the future tense. The building is on fire and the nerds say there will be heat.\n\nThe kitchen said bullwhip. The kitchen said spring loading. The kitchen said face rip. The kitchen said the jawboning is the thing that makes it worse. Rory Johnston said physical markets rip your face off. The nerds said cascading multiplicative effects. Same thesis. Different word count. Some cascading. Some multiplicative. Some bullwhip. Day 27.",
